cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these aggregate results, cite BCI Report and the release you used,
  and cite the upstream dataset each figure was computed on: every dataset page
  at https://bci.report/datasets/ gives its credit line. The licence below covers
  the aggregate measurements this project produced; the underlying recordings
  keep their own terms.
type: dataset
title: "BCI Report: public EEG decoding results reported with their protocol"
abstract: >-
  Cohort-level EEG decoding results, each published with the protocol that
  produced it — cohort, electrode count, evaluation split, chance level,
  interval and known limitations — across motor imagery, SSVEP, P300 and
  semantic ERP, cognitive load, sleep staging, idle false activation, sensor
  and display transfer, movement, calibration budget, foundation-model adaptation (head only, last
  block, LoRA), pretraining controls and a clinical case/control comparison. No raw EEG, no per-participant scores,
  no overall ranking.
authors:
  - name: "BCI Report"
    website: "https://bci.report"
